Installation Instructions for Bellows
=====================================

Copyright (C) 2026 Kival
See the file COPYING for copying conditions.

Basic Installation
------------------

Bellows provides both a top-level GNU-compatible `Makefile` and a
`CMakeLists.txt` build configuration.

To compile all libraries (`libbellows.a` and `libbellows.so`), command-line
programs (`bellows`, `bellows-train`, `bellows-infer`), and the test suite
(`bellows-check`):

    make all

To run the test suite and automated style checks:

    make check

To install the library, headers, pkg-config descriptor (`bellows.pc`), and
executables (optionally specifying `PREFIX` and `DESTDIR`):

    make install PREFIX=/usr/local

To remove all compiled binaries and intermediate files:

    make clean

To package a source distribution tarball:

    make dist
